    "content": "I understand your concern, Maria, and I appreciate you being upfront about wanting to know the root cause. However, I need to be transparent with you about my capabilities.\n\nAs a CRM support agent, I have access to tools for managing individual records (people, companies, opportunities, tasks) and updating relationship metrics, but I don't have access to:\n- System logs or error reports\n- Server status information\n- Bug tracking systems\n- Technical support databases\n- Information about system-wide issues or outages\n\nThe tools available to me are focused on the CRM data itself, not on the underlying system infrastructure or technical issues that might be causing problems.\n\nTo get information about:\n- Whether this is a known bug\n- Server status or outages\n- System-wide issues affecting Innovate Inc. or other users\n- Technical root cause analysis\n\nYou would need to contact:\n1. **Technical Support** - for system-level issues, bugs, or outages\n2. **Your IT department** - if Innovate Inc. has internal systems\n3. **Account Management** - for broader service issues\n4. **System Administrator** - for infrastructure questions\n\nI can help you with:\n- Individual record management (which I've already done)\n- Relationship tracking and metrics\n- Creating/updating opportunities, tasks, and person records\n- Tracking your progress through the sales pipeline\n\nSince you mentioned this is affecting your workflow and you're concerned about recommending the CRM to your team, I'd suggest escalating this technical inquiry to your technical support team or account manager who would have access to system diagnostics and broader issue tracking.\n\nIs there anything else I can help you with regarding your individual CRM records or relationship management?",
